{"name":"Mourning Dove","hex":"#928d88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mourning dove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grey-coloured dove, Zenaida macroura, that has a mournful call, native to North America"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mourning_dove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mourning dove","blocks":[{"text":"The mourning dove is a member of the dove family, Columbidae. The bird is also known as the American mourning dove, the rain dove, and colloquially as the turtle dove, and it was once known as the Carolina pigeon and Carolina turtledove. It is one of the most abundant and widespread North American birds and a popular gamebird, with more than 20 million birds shot annually in the U.S., both for sport and meat. Its ability to sustain its population under such pressure is due to its prolific breeding; in warm areas, one pair may raise up to six broods of two young each in a single year. The wings make an unusual whistling sound upon take-off and landing, a form of sonation. The bird is a strong flier, capable of speeds up to 88 km/h (55 mph)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Mourning_dove_perched_%2861179%29.jpg/330px-Mourning_dove_perched_%2861179%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mourning_dove","wikidata":"Q750027"},{"title":"Mourning Dove (author)","blocks":[{"text":"Mourning Dove or Humishuma was a Native American author, activist, and one of the first Native American women to publish a novel in the United States, best known for her 1927 novel Cogewea, the Half-Blood: A Depiction of the Great Montana Cattle Range and her 1933 work Coyote Stories."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Mourning_Dove_author.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mourning_Dove_(author)","wikidata":"Q11937719"},{"title":"Mourning","blocks":[{"text":"Mourning is the emotional expression in response to a major life event causing grief, especially loss. It typically occurs as a result of someone's death, especially a loved one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Girl_in_mourning_dress_holding_framed_photograph_of_her_father.jpg/330px-Girl_in_mourning_dress_holding_framed_photograph_of_her_father.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mourning","wikidata":"Q750652"},{"title":"Columbidae","blocks":[{"text":"Columbidae is a bird family consisting of doves and pigeons. It is the only family in the order Columbiformes. These are stout-bodied birds with small heads, relatively short necks and slender bills that in some species feature fleshy ceres. They feed largely on plant matter, feeding on seeds (granivory), fruit (frugivory), and foliage (folivory)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg/330px-Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbidae","wikidata":"Q10856"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg/500px-Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg/1280px-Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg/500px-Av_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nominate Z. m. macroura in the Dominican Republic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAv_Mourning_Dove_Caribbean_JG.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg/500px-Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg/1280px-Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg/500px-Zenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Z. m. marginella in California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZenaida_macroura_-California-8-2c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg/500px-Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg/1280px-Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg/500px-Mourning_Dove_%28Zenaida_macroura%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Z. m. carolinensis in Guelph, Ontario, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMourning_Dove_(Zenaida_macroura).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Mourning_Dove_on_fence.jpg/500px-Mourning_Dove_on_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Mourning_Dove_on_fence.jpg/1280px-Mourning_Dove_on_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con